<title>USA: Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 15.</title>
<headline>Canadian Gas Association storage survey - Nov 15.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Canadian Gas Association (CGA) weekly survey of Canadian natural gas in storage in billion cubic feet (bcf):</p>
<p>							 Pct Full  Pct Full</p>
<p>		 11/15/96  11/08/96  Pct Full  Week Ago  Year Ago</p>
<p>East	    215.72    220.14    92.76	94.67     91.80</p>
<p>West	    225.17    228.88    85.02	86.42     78.00</p>
<p>Total Canada  440.89    449.03    88.64	90.28     83.50</p>
<p>East-West division is the Manitoba/Saskatchewan and North Dakota/Minnesota borders.</p>
<p>East capacity 11/15/96: 232.55 bcf, 11/08/96: 232.55 bcf.  </p>
<p>West capacity 11/15/96: 264.84 bcf, 11/08/96: 264.84 bcf.</p>
<p>The Canadian Gas Association survey includes liquefied petroleum gas, all Canadian operators of gas storage and Canadian companies contracting gas storage in the U.S.</p>
<p>-- Reuters Calgary Bureau 403 531-1624</p>
</text>
